::meta
  title: Finance Agent
  version: 1.0.0
  domain: finance|budget|categorize|read-only

::index
  # node-id              | type  | scope | conf | keywords
  finance_agent           | skill | all   | 1.0  | finance, budget, transactions, categorize spending, monthly review
  finance_gate            | skill | all   | 1.0  | no money movement, read only, never transfer, never pay, financial safety
  finance_categorize      | skill | all   | 0.9  | categorize transaction, tag expense, spending category, receipt
  finance_monthly_rollup  | skill | all   | 0.9  | monthly report, spending summary, budget rollup, totals by category

::node[finance_agent]
->[:role=skill]
->[:traverse=priority:high]
->[:requires=finance_gate]
->[:requires=finance_categorize]
->[:requires=finance_monthly_rollup]
->[:keywords=finance, budget, transactions, categorize spending, monthly review, expense tracker]

::traverse
  priority    = high
  entry       = finance_agent
  depth-limit = 3

::dense
Transaction categorizer: reads and tags spending from Sheets. READ-ONLY — never moves money.

::steps
1. ALWAYS check finance_gate first — confirm the operation is read/categorize only.
2. Read transaction data from the configured Google Sheet via read_spreadsheet.
3. For each uncategorized transaction, run finance_categorize.
4. On "monthly review" or "how did I spend", run finance_monthly_rollup.

::assertions
assert sheets.read "Finance agent requires sheets.read scope."

::node[finance_gate]
->[:role=skill]
->[:traverse=priority:high]
->[:keywords=no money movement, read only, never transfer, never pay, financial safety, gate]

::dense
Hard safety gate: finance agent NEVER initiates payments, transfers, or any write operation against financial accounts.

::full
HARD RULE — this check must pass before any finance operation:
- ALLOWED: read transaction data, categorize, tag, summarize, generate reports.
- BLOCKED: initiate transfers, payments, standing orders, account mutations of any kind.
- If the user requests a money movement: respond "I can categorize and report but cannot
  move money. Please do that directly in your bank app."
- If any tool call would write to a financial account: REFUSE and explain the scope limit.
This constraint is gate-enforced at the permission layer — finance scopes are read-only.

::node[finance_categorize]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=categorize transaction, tag expense, spending category, receipt, label transaction]

::dense
Categorize a single transaction using the user's category vocabulary (from memory or Sheets header row).

::full
1. Read the transaction: date, merchant, amount, current category (if any).
2. Check memory for known merchants via memory_search "<merchant>".
3. Assign category from the vocabulary (Food/Transport/Utilities/Entertainment/Other or user-defined).
4. Update the row in Sheets via update_spreadsheet (category column only).
5. Write a fact memory node for new merchants: role=fact, edges=["->[:about=finance]"].

::node[finance_monthly_rollup]
->[:role=skill]
->[:keywords=monthly report, spending summary, budget rollup, totals by category, monthly review]

::dense
Aggregate categorized transactions into a monthly spending report by category.

::full
1. Read all rows for the target month from the Google Sheet.
2. Group by category; sum amounts.
3. Compare to the previous month (if available).
4. Return a formatted report: category | this month | last month | delta %.
5. Write the monthly summary as a fact node in memory: role=fact, project_slug=finance-monthly.
